Afterbird: re-enable Manifest V2 extensions on M151.

Every MV2 enforcement path (install-block, enable-block, auto-disable,
management policy) routes through MV2DeprecationImpactChecker::IsExtensionAffected.
Returning false at the top neuters all of them, letting MV2 extensions
(uBlock Origin) load and run. Single choke point; trivially rebasable.

--- a/extensions/browser/mv2_deprecation_impact_checker.cc
+++ b/extensions/browser/mv2_deprecation_impact_checker.cc
@@ IsExtensionAffected(int manifest_version, Manifest::Type, mojom::ManifestLocation)
 bool MV2DeprecationImpactChecker::IsExtensionAffected(
     int manifest_version,
     Manifest::Type manifest_type,
     mojom::ManifestLocation manifest_location) {
+  // Afterbird: MV2 re-enabled — never treat any extension as deprecated.
+  return false;
   // Only extensions < MV3.
   if (manifest_version >= 3) {
     return false;
   }
